1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,556
When a vulnerable senior faces a night crisis like wandering or a sudden fall, traditional smart home devices leave families in the dark

2
00:00:05,556 --> 00:00:11,112
We built Ring Compass to solve this with touchless spatial safety.

3
00:00:11,112 --> 00:00:19,487
The household needs four answers: 01: is it real? 02: what changed? 03: what do I do? And 04: can I go back to sleep? Current tools answer only the first

4
00:00:19,487 --> 00:00:27,863
Ring Compass answers all four.

5
00:00:27,863 --> 00:00:35,663
Our architecture transforms raw camera feeds into a touchless biometric mesh

6
00:00:35,663 --> 00:00:43,463
OpenCV frames feed our local MCP Spatial Server, where EVM extracts vitals while kinetic tracking detects distress, routing directly to local AI triage and Alexa connected devices.

7
00:00:43,463 --> 00:00:51,371
As documented in our Friction Log, the cloud-side Alexa Plus console restricts developer SDK access

8
00:00:51,371 --> 00:00:59,279
To build with zero AWS cost, we engineered a local Model Context Protocol server running sandboxed JSON-RPC, fully ready for production Alexa Plus.

9
00:00:59,279 --> 00:01:06,275
On our live System Overview console, Ring Compass continuously ingests the hallway camera stream in real time

10
00:01:06,275 --> 00:01:13,271
Scrolling down displays live dispersion cadence, through-lens heart rate, the active Alexa node, and the 2D spatial trajectory plot.

11
00:01:13,271 --> 00:01:19,607
In Motion Analysis, dual cameras monitor corridor and porch feeds simultaneously

12
00:01:19,607 --> 00:01:25,943
Scrolling down to the 2D spatial centroid analysis, coordinate matrices expose the erratic pacing loop

13
00:01:25,943 --> 00:01:32,279
Below it, the chart displays the Disorientation Cadence Index spiking past 3.0, triaging cognitive distress instantly.

14
00:01:32,279 --> 00:01:38,391
How is heartbeat determined through the air? In this EVM breakdown on the abnormal subject in camera two, we isolate forehead pixels to detect sub-visual luminosity shifts

15
00:01:38,391 --> 00:01:44,503
A temporal bandpass filter extracts Heart Rate at 104 BPM and Respiration at 22 RPM

16
00:01:44,503 --> 00:01:50,615
completely touchless.

17
00:01:50,615 --> 00:01:57,971
Our Safety Engine executes a six-stage deterministic gate, triaging between wandering and fall collapse in under 42 milliseconds

18
00:01:57,971 --> 00:02:05,327
In System and Events, an immutable audit trail logs all biometric verdicts and dispatch events with zero cloud data leakage.

19
00:02:05,327 --> 00:02:13,535
When camera two detects a subject collapsing, our engine identifies a vertical drop exceeding 42 pixels, triggering Profile B

20
00:02:13,535 --> 00:02:21,743
The system immediately dispatches an automated emergency email to the caregiver, as verified in this email sent to sanjeevkumaredu8@gmail.com.

21
00:02:21,743 --> 00:02:28,055
Inside Home and Voice, physical de-escalation activates upon crisis detection

22
00:02:28,055 --> 00:02:34,367
Because a commercial smart bulb was unavailable, ambient pathway lighting is simulated via the edge node LED alongside the physical speaker.

23
00:02:34,367 --> 00:02:43,534
[Alexa Connected Hardware Node: Amber LED Glowing · Physical Speaker Beep]

24
00:02:43,534 --> 00:02:50,110
With the grounding alert tone completed and the amber pathway light illuminated, the individual is safely guided back to bed.

25
00:02:50,110 --> 00:02:53,130
To conclude, Ring Compass answers all four questions: Yes, it is real

26
00:02:53,130 --> 00:02:56,150
The spatial cadence changed

27
00:02:56,150 --> 00:02:59,170
Alexa and email autonomously intervened

28
00:02:59,170 --> 00:03:02,190
And yes, you can go back to sleep

29
00:03:02,190 --> 00:03:05,210
All with on-device local privacy and zero cloud costs

30
00:03:05,210 --> 00:03:08,230
Thank you.
